## 🧪 How to Execute Tests

### Quick Start (Recommended Path)

#### Step 1: Environment Setup
```bash
# Option A: On 253 Server (Recommended)
ssh 253
cd ~/freelang-vm
rustup default stable  # One-time setup

# Option B: Local Termux
rustup default stable  # One-time setup
cd /data/data/com.termux/files/home/freelang-vm
```

#### Step 2: Run Tests
```bash
# Full test suite (all 99 tests)
cargo test 2>&1 | tee test_results.log

# Release build (optimized)
cargo test --release 2>&1 | tee test_results_release.log

# Specific test groups
cargo test test_gc_          # GC tests only
cargo test test_compact_     # Compaction tests only
cargo test test_gc test_compact  # All Phase B tests
```

#### Step 3: Run Benchmarks (Optional)
```bash
# If benchmarking crate is available
cargo bench 2>&1 | tee benchmark_results.log

# Individual benchmark
cargo bench allocation
```

#### Step 4: Stress Tests (Optional)
```bash
# Run stress test scenarios
cargo test stress 2>&1 | tee stress_results.log
```

#### Step 5: Generate Report
```bash
# Comprehensive report
echo "=== Phase B Test Report ===" > final_report.txt
echo "Date: $(date)" >> final_report.txt
cargo test 2>&1 >> final_report.txt
```

